## Summary

The task described the CSRF failure as a symptom, but the root cause was in RESTEasy Reactive's core handler wiring, not the CSRF filter itself (the filter's header-verification logic already matched the upstream-fixed version).

**Bug:** In `RuntimeResourceDeployment.java`, the body-reading handlers were wired with an `else if`:

```java
if (method.isFormParamRequired() || hasWithFormReadRequestFilters) {
    handlers.add(new FormBodyHandler(...));   // form parser
} else if (bodyParameter != null) {           // <-- only reached when NO WithFormRead filter
    ... handlers.add(new InputHandler(...));   // raw body reader
}
```

The CSRF filter is annotated `@WithFormRead`, so `hasWithFormReadRequestFilters` is `true` for every endpoint it guards. That took the first branch and — via `else if` — **skipped the `InputHandler` entirely**. `FormBodyHandler`'s parser factory returns `null` for non-form content types (`text/plain`, JSON), so it reads nothing. The reactive endpoint's `String body` parameter therefore arrived empty, and the body never reached the handler.

**Fix:** Split the `else if` into a separate `if`, so a non-form, non-blocking body parameter still gets an `InputHandler`:

```java
if (method.isFormParamRequired() || hasWithFormReadRequestFilters) {
    handlers.add(new FormBodyHandler(...));
}
if (bodyParameter != null) {                   // now independent
    if (!defaultBlocking && !method.isBlocking()) {
        handlers.add(new InputHandler(...));
    }
}
```

This matches the upstream fix (Quarkus 3.9.0+, issue [#38326](https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/38326)). No double-read results: `InputHandler.handle()` returns early when `hasInputStream()` is already true, so form-urlencoded requests (where `FormBodyHandler` sets the stream) are unaffected, while non-form bodies now get read and passed to the endpoint.

**Behavior after the fix, per the requirements:**
- GET token endpoint → 200 + `csrf-token` cookie (unchanged, was already working).
- Form-urlencoded POST → 400 on missing/mismatched form field, 200 on match (unchanged).
- No-body POST → header `X-CSRF-TOKEN` verified: 400 missing/wrong, 200 match (unchanged; header path returns before body handling).
- **Non-form body POST (`text/plain`)** → header verified for 400 cases, and on a valid header the body is now read by `InputHandler` and delivered to the endpoint (200 with echoed body).

The change was confined to source (`RuntimeResourceDeployment.java`); no test files were touched. The module compiles cleanly offline.

